+# Dublin Events Scraper Setup Guide
+
+## Overview
+
+The Dublin Events App includes a **midnight scraper** that automatically updates event listings from 6 major Dublin venues every night at midnight UTC (or configurable time).
+
+## Venues Scraped
+
+1. **Abbey Theatre** (https://www.abbeytheatre.ie) - Theater
+2. **Gaiety Theatre** (https://www.gaietytheatre.ie) - Theater
+3. **Vicar Street** (https://www.vicarstreet.com) - Music/Comedy
+4. **Whelans** (https://www.whelanslive.com) - Music
+5. **Craic Den Comedy Club** (https://www.craicdencomedyclub.com) - Comedy
+6. **3 Arena** (https://www.3arena.ie) - Large Venue/Music
+
+## How It Works
+
+### Scraper Features
+
+- ✅ Real photographic images from venue websites (no placeholders)
+- ✅ Automatic event deduplication (matches by title + date + venue)
+- ✅ Database upsert (inserts new events, updates existing ones)
+- ✅ Image URL validation (venue-domain hosted only)
+- ✅ Comprehensive error handling and logging
+- ✅ Event metadata: title, date, price, description, ticket URL
+
+### Data Pipeline
+
+1. **Scraper runs** → Fetches event data from each venue's What's On page
+2. **Image extraction** → Extracts photographic image URLs from event cards
+3. **Database upsert** → Creates or updates events in PostgreSQL via Prisma
+4. **Deduplication** → Prevents duplicate events from being created
+5. **Source tracking** → Links events to their scraper source for auditing
+
+## Configuration
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+```env
+# Secret key for triggering scrapers (required)
+SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY="your-secret-key-here"
+
+# Timezone for scheduling (optional, defaults to UTC)
+SCRAPER_TIMEZONE="Europe/Dublin"
+```
+
+## Manual Scraper Trigger
+
+### Option 1: Via API Endpoint
+
+Trigger the scraper manually with a POST request:
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST "http://localhost:3000/api/scrape/midnight?key=your-secret-key"
+```
+
+Response example:
+```json
+{
+  "success": true,
+  "message": "✅ All 6 venues scraped successfully! Found 47 events.",
+  "timestamp": "2026-10-01T00:15:30.000Z",
+  "summary": {
+    "totalVenues": 6,
+    "successfulVenues": 6,
+    "failedVenues": 0,
+    "totalEventsScraped": 47,
+    "durationMs": 8250
+  },
+  "results": [
+    {
+      "venue": "Abbey Theatre",
+      "events": 8,
+      "success": true
+    },
+    ...
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### Option 2: Local Development
+
+Run the scraper locally:
+
+```bash
+npm run scraper
+# OR for midnight scraper specifically:
+node -r ts-node/register src/lib/scrapers/midnight-scraper.ts
+```
+
+## Scheduling for Production (Railway)
+
+### Using External Scheduler
+
+Railway doesn't have built-in cron jobs, but you can trigger the scraper endpoint from an external service:
+
+**Option A: EasyCron (Recommended)**
+
+1. Go to https://www.easycron.com/
+2. Create a new cron job:
+   - **URL**: `https://yourapp.railway.app/api/scrape/midnight?key=YOUR_SECRET_KEY`
+   - **Cron Expression**: `0 0 * * *` (midnight UTC)
+   - **Method**: GET or POST
+
+**Option B: GitHub Actions**
+
+Create `.github/workflows/midnight-scrape.yml`:
+
+```yaml
+name: Midnight Scraper
+
+on:
+  schedule:
+    - cron: '0 0 * * *'  # Midnight UTC
+
+jobs:
+  scrape:
+    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
+    steps:
+      - name: Trigger Scraper
+        run: |
+          curl -X POST "${{ secrets.RAILWAY_APP_URL }}/api/scrape/midnight?key=${{ secrets.SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY }}"
+```
+
+**Option C: Railway Scheduled Jobs** (if available in your plan)
+
+Contact Railway support to set up a scheduled job that POSTs to `/api/scrape/midnight`.
+
+## Monitoring & Logging
+
+### View Recent Scraper Runs
+
+The scraper logs to the application's standard output. On Railway, check the deployment logs for scraper execution details.
+
+### Key Metrics to Monitor
+
+- **Events per venue** - Should be 5-15 per venue (varies seasonally)
+- **Scraper duration** - Target: 5-15 seconds for all 6 venues
+- **Success rate** - Should be 100% (6/6 venues successful)
+- **Error rates** - Monitor failed venues and investigate
+
+### Database Queries
+
+Check recent event additions:
+
+```sql
+-- Events added in the last 24 hours
+SELECT venue_id, COUNT(*) as event_count, MAX(created_at) as last_update
+FROM "Event"
+WHERE created_at >= NOW() - INTERVAL '24 hours'
+GROUP BY venue_id
+ORDER BY last_update DESC;
+
+-- All sources and their last scrape time
+SELECT name, url, scraper_type, last_scraped_at
+FROM "Source"
+ORDER BY last_scraped_at DESC;
+```
+
+## Troubleshooting
+
+### Scraper Returns 0 Events
+
+**Causes:**
+- Venue website structure changed (selectors no longer match)
+- Network timeout or proxy issues
+- Venue page requires JavaScript rendering (Cheerio can't execute JS)
+
+**Fix:**
+- Inspect the venue website DOM to find new CSS selectors
+- Update selectors in `src/lib/scrapers/sites/EnhancedTheaterScraper.ts`
+- Re-test with: `curl "http://localhost:3000/api/scrape?key=your-key"`
+
+### Images Not Displaying
+
+**Causes:**
+- Image URL not venue-domain hosted (external CDN blocked by proxy)
+- Image URL malformed (missing protocol or base URL)
+
+**Fix:**
+- Verify image URLs start with `https://www.venuename.ie/...`
+- Check database: `SELECT image_url FROM "Event" LIMIT 5;`
+- Manually inspect venue website for valid image URLs
+
+### Scraper Timeout
+
+**Causes:**
+- Venue website is slow or unresponsive
+- Network issues
+- Too many concurrent scraper requests
+
+**Fix:**
+- Increase timeout in `/api/scrape/midnight/route.ts` `maxDuration`
+- Stagger scraper runs (run one venue at a time instead of parallel)
+- Check network connectivity to venue websites
+
+## Event Deduplication Logic
+
+Events are matched using this criteria:
+
+- **Title** (case-insensitive)
+- **Start Date** (within ±1 minute window)
+- **Venue** (exact match)
+
+If all three match, the event is considered a duplicate and NOT created again. This prevents duplicate entries when the scraper runs multiple times.
+
+## API Response Fields
+
+Each scraped event includes:
+
+```typescript
+{
+  title: string              // Event name
+  description?: string       // Event details
+  dateStart: Date           // Event start time
+  dateEnd?: Date            // Event end time (if known)
+  genre: string             // Category (Theater, Music, Comedy, etc.)
+  ticketPriceMin?: number   // Lowest ticket price
+  ticketPriceMax?: number   // Highest ticket price
+  ticketUrl?: string        // Link to buy tickets
+  imageUrl?: string         // Photo of event (venue-domain hosted)
+  venueName: string         // Venue name
+  sourceUrl: string         // URL scraped from
+  sourceEventId?: string    // Unique ID from source
+}
+```
+
+## Development Notes
+
+### Adding New Venues
+
+To add another Dublin venue:
+
+1. Create a new scraper class extending `EnhancedTheaterScraper`
+2. Add it to the scrapers array in `/src/lib/scrapers/midnight-scraper.ts`
+3. Inspect the venue's website and set correct CSS selectors
+4. Test locally: `curl "http://localhost:3000/api/scrape?key=dev-scraper-key"`
+
+Example:
+
+```typescript
+export class NewVenueScraper extends EnhancedTheaterScraper {
+  constructor() {
+    super(
+      'New Venue Name',
+      'https://www.newvenue.ie',
+      '.event-card, [data-event]',  // Event container selectors
+      'img, [data-image]'             // Image selectors
+    )
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### Testing Image Extraction
+
+The scraper logs which events had images extracted. Check logs for:
+
+```
+✅ Abbey Theatre: Parsed event: "ANIMALS" on 10/23/2026 (with image)
+```
+
+Missing "(with image)" means the image selector didn't find an image URL.
+
+## Next Steps
+
+1. ✅ Deploy the app to Railway
+2. ✅ Set up SCRAPER_SECRET_KEY in Railway environment variables
+3. ✅ Configure EasyCron or GitHub Actions for midnight triggers
+4. ✅ Monitor the first scraper run and adjust selectors if needed
+5. ✅ Set up logging/alerts for failed venues
+
+---
